# @ f_ormat< "text {expr}" interpolates: each {expr} is any expression,
# written as f_ormat writes its value; {{ and }} are braces (MC24,
# Rust's format!).
== SOURCE
x := 6
n := 3 4
@ f_ormat< "x = {x}, twice {x * 2}, n = {n} {{braces}}"
p_rint! @ f_ormat< "plain"
== EXPAND
x := 6
n := 3 4
"x = " c_at (f_ormat (x)) c_at ", twice " c_at (f_ormat (x * 2)) c_at ", n = " c_at (f_ormat (n)) c_at " {" c_at "braces}"
p_rint! ("plain")
== RESULT
x = 6, twice 12, n = 3 4 {braces}
plain
plain
